# Build context hygiene, and one security rule.
#
# backend/.env is gitignored, so Render - which builds from the repo - never
# sees it. A local `docker build` does, and `COPY backend ./backend` would bake
# a live session secret and access code into an image layer where it survives
# every later deletion. Excluded here so the two build paths cannot disagree
# about that.
.env
backend/.env

# The world is seeded during the build. Shipping the local 321MB copy into the
# context as well just makes the upload slow and the layer wrong.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
*.md
